---
scope: src/tools/info
status: aligned
description: "Boot-time reporter that returns AIDE artifact staleness and brain-precondition state in one read-only pass so the orchestrator can branch on each before pipeline work runs."
intent: >
  aide_info is the passive precondition reporter the orchestrator calls
  during its boot sequence. It returns two structurally different
  findings as independent fields — artifact staleness and brain
  configuration state — so the orchestrator can apply different
  policies to each. Brain detection is forwarded unchanged from the
  upstream detector; this tool composes nothing, mutates nothing, and
  surfaces no path-validation state. All pre-init and misconfiguration
  conditions resolve to structured states, never thrown errors, so the
  first-ever boot on a cold project completes cleanly.
outcomes:
  desired:
    - Returns artifact staleness and brain-precondition state as two independent top-level fields, so the orchestrator can branch on each without scanning the other.
    - Treats artifact staleness as a soft notification — the orchestrator may advise the user but the pipeline can still run when artifacts are outdated.
    - Treats brain-precondition state as a hard gate — any non-ok brain state halts the orchestrator until the user runs the visible remediation command.
    - Forwards the upstream brain detector's tagged result unchanged; the closed status vocabulary it defines is the only vocabulary this tool surfaces.
    - Resolves every pre-init and misconfiguration condition (missing config, unreadable wiring, drift) to a structured state, never a thrown error.
  undesired:
    - Throwing or erroring on a cold project where brain configuration and the host's wiring file have never been written. First-ever boot must complete cleanly.
    - Returning a pre-formatted message instead of structured state. Message composition belongs to the orchestrator, which tailors wording to the user's session context.
    - Conflating artifact staleness with brain-precondition state — folding them into a single verdict, sentinel value, or shared array. Their severities differ and the orchestrator branches on each separately.
    - Auto-repairing drift, auto-syncing the host's wiring, or otherwise mutating any file the user owns. The boot reporter is read-only; remediation flows through the user's visible command boundary.
    - Surfacing a status that names launcher-path validity. Path resolution is the launcher's responsibility at MCP server startup, not this reporter's.
    - Extending the brain status vocabulary beyond what the upstream detector defines, including renames or aliases of retired states. The detector is the single source of truth for the closed set.
---
